description:
Design a circuit that implements a one-bit XOR gate using only NOR gates. The module takes two input signals, a and b, and produces an output that is true (high) if exactly one of the inputs is true, effectively demonstrating the functionality of an XOR operation. The design leverages various configurations of NOR gates to construct equivalent NOT, NAND, and ultimately the XOR logic, ensuring the output reflects the XOR truth table.
module top_module(
  input a,
  input b,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input a,
  input b,
  output out
);wire na, nb, nand1, nand2, nand3, nand4;

  // Implementing NOT gates using NOR gates
  nor(na, a, a);
  nor(nb, b, b);

  // Implementing NAND gates using NOR gates
  nor(nand1, a, nb);
  nor(nand2, na, b);

  // Implementing OR gate using NOR gates
  nor(nand3, nand1, nand2);

  // Implementing NOT gate using NOR gate
  nor(nand4, nand3, nand3);

  // Output of XOR gate
  assign out = nand4;

endmodule

