description:
Design a 1-to-8 de-serializer that takes a single serial input bit and converts it into an 8-bit parallel output. The output is updated on the rising edge of the clock signal. A reset signal initializes the count, which tracks the number of received bits. The de-serializer captures the serial input bit into the appropriate position of the output based on the current count value, effectively translating a sequence of serial bits into a complete byte once eight bits have been received.
module top_module(in,out,clk,reset
    );

code:
module top_module(in,out,clk,reset
    );input in,clk,reset;
output reg[7:0]out;
reg [3:0]count;
always@(posedge clk or negedge reset)begin
if(~reset)count<=0;
else begin
	if(count<=7)begin
	count<=count+1;
	end
	else begin
	count<=1;
	end
end
end
always@(count)begin
out[count-1]=in;
end
endmodule

