Design a 16-bit shift register that captures a 4-bit input value on each clock cycle and shifts the stored data left by one position. Each of the four bits of the input feeds into the least significant bit of the shift register in sequential clock cycles. The output reflects the current state of the shift register, providing a delay mechanism for the incoming data over multiple clock cycles.
