description:
Design a 32-bit bit-shifter that performs left or right bit shifts on a 32-bit input based on a 5-bit control signal. If the control signal `n` is positive, it executes a left shift by `n` bits; if `n` is negative (or zero), it performs an arithmetic right shift by the absolute value of `n`, adjusting the output to zero when `n` exceeds 31. If `n` equals zero, the output remains unchanged, effectively allowing for variable shifting of the input data.
module top_module(
  input [31:0] a,
  input [4:0] n,
  output [31:0] b
);

