description:
Design a frequency divider that takes a 12MHz input clock and outputs a 1Hz clock signal. The module uses a counter to divide the input clock frequency by a parameterized value "M," which is set to 12 by default. The most significant bit of the counter serves as the output clock signal (clk_out), effectively generating a lower frequency clock by toggling once every M clock cycles of the input signal. This configuration is commonly used in digital circuits to derive slower clock signals from a faster one.
module top_module(
  input wire clk_in,
  output wire clk_out
);

