description:
Design a 4-bit binary counter that increments its count on each rising edge of the clock signal (clk). Upon receiving a reset signal (rst), the counter resets to zero. The current count is output as a 4-bit wide value, allowing the counting of values from 0 to 15.
module top_module(
    clk,
    rst,
    count
);

code:
module top_module(
    clk,
    rst,
    count
);input clk;
input rst;
output reg [3:0] count;

always @(posedge clk, posedge rst) begin
    if (rst) begin
        count <= 4'b0;
    end else begin
        count <= count + 1;
    end
end

endmodule

